From 99bcb001d54727f2b7c64a47d9f567ab7abaa3f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:44:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] plugin_api: keep a pixel plugin running across a rotation

Rotating from Quick Settings returns AERA to Home, which ends a running
pixel plugin: its surface had one fixed size, so there was no way to
give it the new shape.

Size the surface memfd at launch for either orientation (pages are only
allocated where the plugin draws) and, when the screen's size changes,
lay the scene out again and send a new SURFACE with the rotated size on
the same fd. Each SURFACE starts a generation, which PRESENT carries in
`flags` (0 for the first, so current plugins are unaffected); a frame
drawn for an earlier generation goes straight back with FRAME_DONE
instead of being shown at the wrong size. After a new SURFACE every slot
is the plugin's again, and the scene shows nothing until a frame of the
new shape arrives. The rotation toggle no longer returns Home while a
pixel plugin is running.

The Quick Settings shade the rotation was started from stays open over
the plugin, so it is laid out again for the screen's new size instead of
keeping the old orientation's width (tiles cut off at the edge).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01J6XhHxrkhAcXmkzHMeCnVz
